        "id": "ch12_2-1",
        "text": "Understanding Linux containers\nAs we have demonstrated in the previous chapter, there are two main types of virtualization: virtual\nmachine ( VM ) -based and container-based . We discussed VM-based virtualization in the previous\nchapter, and now it is time to explain what containers are. At a very basic, conceptual level, containers\nare similar to VMs. They have similar purposes \u2013 allowing an isolated environment to run \u2013 but they\nare different in so many ways that they can hardly be called similar. Let\u2019s compare these two concepts\nin more detail.\nManaging Containers with Docker\n446\nEsta secci\u00f3n contiene las siguientes subsecciones\n\u2022 Comparing containers and VMs\n\u2022 Understanding the underlying container technology\n\u2022 Understanding Docker\nSi deseas explorar cualquiera de estas subsecciones, puedes pregunt\u00e1rmelo directamente.",
